From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nassos Yiannopoulos <nassosyian@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hw/display/pvg: no dmabuf on Windows

With a GL display the device registered the console with GL ops, which
declare dmabuf scanout; Windows displays have no dmabufs and console setup
failed ("The console requires display DMABUF support"). On Windows the
dmabuf property is forced off: presents take the CPU path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 hw/display/pvg-linux-pci.c |    3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/display/pvg-linux-pci.c b/hw/display/pvg-linux-pci.c
index 3120151..a5e75a7 100644
--- a/hw/display/pvg-linux-pci.c
+++ b/hw/display/pvg-linux-pci.c
@@ -2801,6 +2801,9 @@ static void pvg_linux_realize(PCIDevice *dev, Error **errp)
     if (s->guest_fixups_enable) {
         s->guest_fixups = pvg_guest_fixups_start(pvg_exec_log, s);
     }
+#ifdef _WIN32
+    s->dmabuf = false;      /* no dmabufs on Windows: GL displays get CPU-path surfaces too */
+#endif
     if (s->display_ports) {
         s->con = qemu_graphic_console_create(DEVICE(dev), 0,
                                              s->dmabuf && display_opengl &&
-- 
2.43.0

